{"id": 9058, "name": "Hythe Municipal Campground", "read": "2026-10-15", "pages": [{"url": "https://www.countygp.ab.ca/parks-recreation-community/campgrounds-parks-trails-and-playgrounds/hythe-municipal-campground/", "lines": [" Section Menu | | Campgrounds open for the summer season on Friday, May 15th, 2026 | Summer DAY-USE hours are from 7:00AM - 11:00PM from May 15, 2026 - October 15, 2026 | | | | Address: 10004 104th Street, Hythe, AB | A $7 nightly fire permit fee will be in place at all County campgrounds to supplement the costs of firewood handling and firepit safety maintenance. | $45 / night for full service (power, water, sewer) ", " - October 15, 2026 | | | | Address: 10004 104th Street, Hythe, AB | A $7 nightly fire permit fee will be in place at all County campgrounds to supplement the costs of firewood handling and firepit safety maintenance. | $45 / night for full service (power, water, sewer) plus $7 fire permit fee / night. $5 online reservation fee / booking | $29 / night for no service overflow area plus $7 fire permit fee / night. $5 o", "County campgrounds to supplement the costs of firewood handling and firepit safety maintenance. | $45 / night for full service (power, water, sewer) plus $7 fire permit fee / night. $5 online reservation fee / booking | $29 / night for no service overflow area plus $7 fire permit fee / night. $5 online reservation fee / booking | $5 for non-campers using the dump station | Camping fees include firewood and use of the"]}, {"url": "https://www.countygp.ab.ca/home-property-environment/animal-services/", "lines": [], "via": "Animal Services"}, {"url": "https://www.countygp.ab.ca/council-administration/bylaws-and-policies/bylaw-and-enforcement-services/", "lines": [], "via": "Enforcement Services"}, {"url": "https://www.countygp.ab.ca/home-property-environment/fire-services/", "lines": [], "via": "Fire Services"}, {"url": "https://www.countygp.ab.ca/home-property-environment/water-and-sewer-services/", "lines": ["hat is changing for residential and commercial customers in County hamlets? | County residential and commercial water and sewer customers will see an increase on their bills in May 2026. County residential water will be $75 monthly ($150 bi-monthly) and sewer will be $50 monthly ($100 bi-monthly). | The commercial rates for water will be $350 bi-monthly and commercial sewer will increase to $150 bi-monthly (Level 1),", "d sewer customers will see an increase on their bills in May 2026. County residential water will be $75 monthly ($150 bi-monthly) and sewer will be $50 monthly ($100 bi-monthly). | The commercial rates for water will be $350 bi-monthly and commercial sewer will increase to $150 bi-monthly (Level 1), $200 bi-monthly (Level 2), and $300 bi-monthly (Level 3). The new rates will be reflected on your March - April 2026 bi", "on their utility bills instead of being paid from general taxes. | Is this increase due to the County's capital plan for utilities? | No. The County’s 10-year Water and Sewer Capital Plan for hamlet systems, worth about $30 million, is funded through the County’s capital budget and external grants, not through utility rates. The changes to flat rate charges are about recovering some operating costs, not infrastructur", "rates charged in other hamlets | How do the new water and sewer rates compare to other nearby municipalities? | A review of seven similar municipalities shows an average monthly residential water and sewer bill of about $130.59, with municipal fixed (flat) delivery costs typically ranging from roughly $71 to $96 per month, depending on the system. | The County compared its rates to regional municipalities including S"], "via": "Water and Sewer Services"}]}
